# meta-deploy.list: the queue meta-deploy.bash runs, in this order.
#
# STANDING RULE (CLAUDE/AgentNotes.md): this list is exactly what needs running NOW. Add a
# run when it is pending, remove it once it has run and is done, leave out what cannot
# usefully run yet, then ask the owner to run meta-deploy.bash. Every step a run needs lives
# in the plan's own scripts, so this is the only command the owner is handed. The order is by
# dependency. A plan with none of triage.bash, deploy.bash and acceptance.bash has nothing
# for the script to do. A triage-only plan is run once, read-only. Words after the folder
# name are passed to that plan's triage.bash, both runs.
#
# One entry per line, four kinds:
#   <plan folder>                  its triage, deploy and acceptance scripts, in order
#   playbooks/<path>.yml           a change no plan owns; run as one unit through its own
#                                  shebang, which goes through run.bash, exactly as
#                                  ./playbooks/imports/<play>.yml does by hand
#   <plan folder>/<script>.bash    one plan script, for a step none of the three fixed names
#                                  fits; run as one unit, like a playbook entry, except
#                                  that a script named *acceptance*.bash may exit 2 for
#                                  COULD NOT ESTABLISH, as an acceptance.bash may
#   changed-plays                  every play that has run here and has to run again, as
#                                  one unit: the checkout's ./run.bash --changed --yes, in
#                                  playbook-main.yml order, stopping at the first failure
#
# changed-plays runs WHERE IT STANDS in the list, like every other entry, and decides which
# plays it runs when it starts, so the entries above it have already run (a play an entry
# above ran is no longer changed, and is not run twice). Put it above the plan entries whose
# deploy or acceptance expects the changed plays to have run, which is the usual case, and
# below an entry it must follow. It replaces a hand-copied list of stale plays: name a
# playbooks/ entry only for a play that must run at a fixed point between two plan steps.
# Its description says which changed plays the agent expects it to pick up and why.
#
# A line starting with # is a comment and is the description of the entry below it: it is how
# the owner learns what a run will do, so write it. Blank lines are ignored. Any other line
# that is not an entry is a fatal error naming its line number.

# The changed plays are named one by one, not run as changed-plays: changed-plays stops at its
# first failure, and play-podman.yml comes first and fails on purpose until the old-range files
# in the podman store are dealt with (Plan 00235 Q6, now triaged case by case below), so none
# of the others would run. play-podman.yml runs in the 00235 entry. play-claude-code-consumer.yml
# imports play-podman.yml, so it waits too.
# URGENT, issue #115/#116: CCY 3.103.2, container 2.79.16. pingbus reads a sync gap past 20 pages
# from its newest end instead of failing, so a member offline for hours hears its team again (a
# stuck ccy member recovers once its session is restarted on the new image). Also from CCY 3.103.1:
# a token with no usage left is refused in a red banner on a terminal (Plan 00191
# Task 4.7); every image ccy builds is labelled ccy-version, and a build removes project images
# an older ccy built (Plan 00235 Q7; it removes nothing while the store-clean marker is absent,
# as it is now); lxc-add's new gh login message (Plan 00177 Task 9.5). Rebuilds
# claude-yolo:latest, ccy-sessions and ccy-token-usable. Nothing is asked.
playbooks/imports/play-claude-yolo.yml
# The same pingbus gap fix in the member kit LXC and host members run. Plan 00177 Task 9.5: the
# LXC member join installs gh in each declared running container where
# it is missing (GitHub's apt or dnf repository, or Alpine's github-cli), then stops with one
# message naming the gh device-code login command for each agent user not yet logged in.
playbooks/imports/play-agent-bus.yml
# Plan 00192 Task 3.16: the camera hotspot Wi-Fi password is no longer asked for. With none
# saved, the play makes a three-word one, vaults it and keeps it on later runs; ftp-camera
# shows the network name and password whenever the hotspot is up. Rebuilds the ftp-camera tool.
# It may restart vsftpd: if the owner is uploading photos, hold this run until they are done.
playbooks/imports/optional/common/play-ftp-camera.yml
# Rebuilds the nordvpn-openvpn tool (Go). Nothing else changes.
playbooks/imports/optional/common/play-nordvpn-openvpn.yml
# Rebuilds wsi and the speech-to-text panel extension and its schema: the model manager says
# "Checking the GPU and the models..." on its first frame and its GPU line reads clearly (Plan
# 00234 Tasks 2.4-2.5); a notification when recorded files start and finish transcribing,
# behind the new "Notify on file transcription" switch (Plan 00179 Task 4.5). The extension
# changes take effect after the owner logs out and in.
playbooks/imports/optional/common/play-speech-to-text.yml
# Plan 00234: the model manager's screen check (read only), now waiting for the checking line.
00234-stt-model-manager-fits-gpu/acceptance.bash
# Plan 00198 (Complete): the Text Editor override moved to play-gnome-shell.yml beside the
# editor's install, unchanged; expect no change to the per-user desktop file.
playbooks/imports/play-gnome-shell.yml
# Plan 00228 Task 6.7: the consumer VM scenario installs speech-to-text. deploy.bash runs
# play-vm-test-lab.yml (asks for sudo once): it rebuilds vmtest (also Plan 00192 Tasks
# 3.13-3.15: a failed member-up prints the end of the guest's console log; the SSH wait is
# settable by VMTEST_SSH_WAIT_TIMEOUT), and deploys the manifest and its checker (20 checks).
# acceptance.bash then runs desktop-consumer-install, desktop-fresh-install and
