# HEAD is not pushed); the consumer run is long, as speech-to-text downloads its models.
00228-consumer-install-without-github
# Plan 00201 Task 2.7, ACCEPTANCE-owner.md step 08: cc --teams's Element consent, No then Yes,
# driven in a private tmux on two throwaway teams (consent201a, consent201b) in a scratch
# checkout, all removed after. Holds ~/.config/pingbus/element-accepted aside and puts it back
# however the run ends (and puts back first what a killed run left). Prompts for sudo once; if
# sudo also asks inside the private tmux, it prints how to attach and waits (exit 2 if nobody
# types it). Exit 2 is COULD NOT ESTABLISH.
00201-ccy-teams-many-teams-per-session-descriptions-and-a-picker/acceptance-consent.bash
# Plan 00235: triage.bash --du (read only), then deploy.bash (asks for sudo once):
# play-podman.yml repairs the store as root if needed (it removes c/storage's leftover
# temp-dir-N, refusing while podman or buildah is busy), rebuilds container-images, and its root
# probe still finds old-range files, so it keeps container-images-prune.timer stopped and
# disabled and FAILS ON PURPOSE with the Q6 message, as last time. The opt-in podman system
# reset block is gone (the owner: no reset, ever). Acceptance is skipped as the deploy fails.
00235-podman-images-cleaned-up-automatically --du
# Plan 00235 Task 4.7d, the owner's Q6 answer (case by case, no reset): the old-range triage of
# the rootless podman store, read only: a root scan and the user's triage. Its report and the
# proposed decisions (REMOVE, RE-OWN, ASK, HELD per item) are in its run directory; the host
# agent reads them, writes untracked/plan-00235/old-range-decisions.tsv, and the next run's
# dry run and old-range-apply.bash are queued after that.
00235-podman-images-cleaned-up-automatically/old-range.bash
